status: FAIL

findings:
- The revision 11 package materially closes the three prior P0s and most prior P1/P2/P3 findings: cancellation is consistently split between single-frame answer and explicit-frame-list answer_batch; the five numeric-zero owner classes are disclosed; freeze status now gates all three reviews while allowing an implementation; identifier, negotiation, response-ceiling, budget, failed-stream, registry, reserved-seam, ADR, appendix-order, and campaign fixes are present.
- P1: Section 1 assigns conflicting errors to the envelope epoch. SMP1.md:69-73 first includes epoch among failures producing PROTOCOL_FRAME_INVALID, then immediately assigns a non-protocol envelope epoch PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED. The implementation chooses VERSION_UNSUPPORTED at lib.rs:1172-1174. A frozen decoder contract cannot assign two codes to the same defect.
- P1: The claimed per-frame version rule is not reachable through the wire decoder. SMP1 requires a frame below the selected version to emit PROTOCOL_DOWNGRADE and a frame above it to emit PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED. ProtocolFrame::validate rejects every protocol_version unequal to the compile-time PROTOCOL_VERSION as VERSION_UNSUPPORTED (lib.rs:996-999); answer_batch decodes before dispatch (server.rs:324-347), so dispatch's SelectedProfile::check_claim (server.rs:532-540) never sees a below-selection wire frame. The added codec test itself pins both 0 and 2 to VERSION_UNSUPPORTED. Prior P1-3 is therefore not closed by the implementation evidence claimed in the handoff.
- P1: ProtocolFailure.details remains internally contradictory. The normative record says details is "the owner's frozen failure record" (SMP1.md:346), while the new mapping says it is transport-supplied UTF-8 reason bytes, never owner records, restricted to five values (SMP1.md:388-393). This leaves wire decoding and ownership ambiguous.
- P2: The checker does not actually pin retryability lists equal as claimed. check_smp1_contract.py:179-186 only verifies that every server-listed token appears somewhere in the whole spec; it neither extracts the contract's exact enumerations nor rejects contract-only extras, and the AfterCapability check at :187-188 is only a source substring. Current lists agree, but drift in the contract can still pass, so prior checker-coverage P2-6 is only partially closed.
- P3: The revision 11 status is dated 2026-09-06 (SMP1.md:3) although this package and review are on 2026-09-05; the revision is future-dated.

